                <pb facs="0351" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg267"/>

                <head>No. 113.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Beach.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 25,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>If Santos is released let him return in Iroquois. Pending the action of
                    Ecuadorian Congress do not deliver letter.</p>
                <closer><signed>BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
